---
export const title = 'Keyboard, events and forms';
export const order = 300;
---

<p>
  The listbox follows the WAI-ARIA listbox pattern: <code>role="listbox"</code>
  (with <code>aria-multiselectable</code>), options with
  <code>role="option"</code> and <code>aria-selected</code>. It is one tab
  stop. <kbd>Up</kbd> and <kbd>Down</kbd> move between options,
  <kbd>Home</kbd> and <kbd>End</kbd> to the first and last, and typing a
  letter moves to the next option starting with it. Disabled options are
  skipped.
</p>
<ul>
  <li>In a single listbox the selection follows focus.</li>
  <li>
    With <code>multiple</code>, moving does not select: <kbd>Space</kbd> or a
    click toggles the focused option, and <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>A</kbd>
    (<kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>A</kbd>) selects all options, or clears them when all
    are selected.
  </li>
</ul>
<p>
  Every change by the person fires <code>change</code>, which bubbles, with
  <code>detail.value</code> (and <code>detail.values</code> with
  <code>multiple</code>). Setting <code>value</code> from code fires nothing.
</p>
<p>
  The listbox is a form control: it submits under <code>name</code>,
  <code>required</code> blocks submission until an option is chosen,
  <code>disabled</code> and <code>readonly</code> stop the person from changing
  it, and <code>form.reset()</code> restores the starting value.
</p>
